Scenity includes and uses third-party software. Each part keeps its own licence. `bun tools/licences.ts` checks the
licence of each installed package. It also checks that this file names each runtime dependency of the workspace
packages.

Code that a built page holds (vendored files)
---------------------------------------------

- packages/render/src/vendor/GLTFLoader.js: a trimmed copy of three/examples/jsm/loaders/GLTFLoader.js from
  three.js. MIT licence, copyright 2010-2026 three.js authors.
- packages/render/src/vendor/basis_transcoder.js: the Basis Universal transcoder with its Emscripten glue, from
  three/examples/jsm/libs/basis. Apache License 2.0, copyright 2019-2026 Binomial LLC.
- packages/render/src/vendor/GLTFLoaderGeneric.js: the generic trimmed copy of three/examples/jsm/loaders/GLTFLoader.js
  from three.js. MIT licence, copyright 2010-2026 three.js authors.
- packages/render/src/vendor/draco_wasm_wrapper.js: the Draco decoder with its Emscripten glue, from
  three/examples/jsm/libs/draco/gltf, as an ES module. The scene pages also serve its draco_decoder.wasm.
  Apache License 2.0, copyright 2017 The Draco Authors (Google LLC).
- packages/render/src/dracoDecoder.ts: the geometry code of three/examples/jsm/loaders/DRACOLoader.js, in TypeScript.
  MIT licence, copyright 2010-2026 three.js authors.
- packages/render/src/smaaPassGl.ts: the SMAAPass of three/examples/jsm/postprocessing/SMAAPass.js with one change
  (the area and search textures through createImageBitmap). MIT licence, copyright 2010-2026 three.js authors.
- packages/render/src/aoDenoise.ts: the PoissonDenoiseShader of three/examples/jsm/shaders/PoissonDenoiseShader.js as
  a node. MIT licence, copyright 2010-2026 three.js authors.

